script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'auditar-adr121',
  description: 'Adversarial read-only review of W1, not-G, E10 and Tarski modules (ADR-121) and the ADR-120 promotion',
  phases: [{ title: 'Refutar', detail: 'independent lenses try to refute the new headline theorems' }],
}
const R = 'E:/dropbox/github/lean4/ROBINSON_PlusPlus'
const COMMON = `Repository: ${R} (Lean 4 v4.31, no Mathlib). New build modules, compiled locally TODAY by the main session (lake build green, leanchecker green, all #print axioms = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]):
- ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/ModeloCodigo.lean, ModeloEstandar.lean, ModeloCodificacion.lean, SolidezPrf.lean, Consistencia.lean (ADR-120: a model MNV V0 of the 142 axioms; consistencia : ConsistentH; goedel_I : not Prf godelCN; goedel_II : not Prf consistencyFormula'; V0_eq_codigo).
- ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/SolidezVerificador.lean (ADR-121: a total decoder dec : Nat -> Formula, verificador_solido (W1), goedel_I_neg : not Prf (neg godelCN), godelCN_verdadera, con_verdadera).
- ROBINSON_PlusPlus/Meta/TarskiPrf.lean (ADR-121: prf_diagonal, prf_tarski, tarski, tarski_prf_sentences, tarski_semantico).
HARD RULES: NEVER run lake, lean, elan, leanchecker or any build, in Windows or WSL. Read-only: do not edit files. Use Read/Grep/Glob and read-only shell/git only. Report in Spanish. Be ADVERSARIAL: try to REFUTE that the statements mean what their names and docstrings claim; report a concern only with file:line evidence; mark MEASURED vs INFERRED.`
const SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: {
  lens: { type: 'string' }, verdict: { type: 'string', description: 'refutado | sostenido | sostenido-con-reservas' },
  findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
    claim: { type: 'string' }, severity: { type: 'string', description: 'critico | medio | menor' },
    evidence: { type: 'string' }, measured: { type: 'boolean' }, fix: { type: 'string' } },
    required: ['claim', 'severity', 'evidence', 'measured'] } },
  summary: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['lens', 'verdict', 'findings', 'summary'] }
const LENSES = [
  { key: 'goedelI', prompt: `LENS: Goedel I in full. Check that goedel_I (Meta/Consistencia.lean) and goedel_I_neg (Meta/SolidezVerificador.lean) are about the SAME sentence godelCN (Meta/DiagonalNumeral.lean) and the SAME calculus Prf (Meta/Hilbert.lean), that neg is FOL's negation, and that goedel_I_neg's proof uses only: soundness (prf_sound), the fixed point prf_godelCN_fixedpoint, ev_provCodeC' (evaluation of provCodeC' in the model), W1 (verificador_solido) and dec_codeNat. Check that ev_provCodeC' really evaluates ROBINSON_PlusPlus.Meta.ProofChain.provCodeC' (the predicate in the fixed point) and that formCodeM_eq bridges formCode/formCodeM. Check godelCN_verdadera/con_verdadera statements. Look for any autoImplicit capture, shadowed names, or a statement weaker than its docstring.` },
  { key: 'W1', prompt: `LENS: W1 (verificador_solido) and the decoder. Read Meta/SolidezVerificador.lean §1-§4 and the verifier axioms in Minimal/Axioms.lean (ax_lineWF_*, ax_premsOf_*, ax_chainOk_*, ax_runFn_*). Argue whether verificador_solido's statement (chainOkN V0 0 p -> memN y (runFnN 0 p) -> Prf (dec y)) is what 'the arithmetized verifier is sound in the standard model' should mean, and whether the 21 per-rule lemmas (linea_*) match the 21 rules (tags 0..20, incl. thy via V0_eq_codigo, mp and gen via the accumulator invariant Bueno). Check that dec really mirrors substfcN/liftfcN (Meta/ModeloCodigo.lean) so the commutation lemmas are not vacuous, and that dec_codeNat makes dec a left inverse of codeNat. Check the docstrings of the module against the code.` },
  { key: 'tarski', prompt: `LENS: Tarski (Meta/TarskiPrf.lean). Check prf_diagonal is a genuine diagonal lemma for an ARBITRARY formula P (statement: Prf (selfAppN (diagBeta P) iff substFormula 0 (numeral (codeNat (selfAppN (diagBeta P)))) P)), that liar/prf_liar/prf_tarski/tarski/tarski_prf_sentences/tarski_semantico state the standard results (syntactic undefinability: no Tr with Prf (Tr(code phi) iff phi) for all phi; semantic: no Tr defines truth in MNV V0), that IsSentence (liftFormula 0 phi = phi) is a sensible notion of sentence and liftFormula 1 Tr = Tr means 'at most #0 free', and that the negative control example is right. Also check the docstrings.` },
  { key: 'promocion', prompt: `LENS: the ADR-120 promotion and the controls. Compare the five modules with sondeos/ModeloNat.lean (the sondeo they came from) for any semantic difference in definitions (MNV, lineWFT, V0, stepT, premsOfN) or theorem statements; check the new rows in check-footprints.bash and the soundness column in check-estratos.bash (Prf -> ROBINSON_PlusPlus.Meta.SolidezPrf.prf_sound, Prf_i -> ...prfI_sound), the EV_TOK extension and autotest in check-sorry.bash, and that the scoped/local macros cannot leak a reserved keyword to importers (sondeos import ROBINSON_PlusPlus). Check REFERENCE.md catalog rows 84r-84x and DECISIONS.md ADR-120/121 claims against the code.` },
]
phase('Refutar')
const res = await parallel(LENSES.map(l => () => agent(`${COMMON}\n\n${l.prompt}`, { label: `refutar:${l.key}`, phase: 'Refutar', schema: SCHEMA })))
return res.filter(Boolean)
